From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ad5xrecon <ad5xrecon@localhost>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wizard, settings: AD5X nozzle size

A "Nozzle Size" step follows the time zone among the AD5X setup steps, in
the first-start wizard and in "Run Setup Wizard" sessions, where Klipper
has the ad5x_nozzle object. It offers the object's sizes with the running
one selected. Next with another size sends SET_NOZZLE_SIZE, which restarts
Klipper, and holds the wizard (new Step::hold_on_next() hook, resumed with
ui_wizard_advance()) until Klipper is ready again with that size, so the
tuning steps never start against a restarting Klipper. A refusal, or no
Klipper within a minute, shows the reason with Retry and Skip. When
local.cfg sets the size the dropdown is fixed and says so.

Settings > Printer gets a "Nozzle Size" row with the current size, shown
only with the object. It opens a chooser that asks first (Klipper
restarts), is locked during a print and points to local.cfg when that
sets the size. The object joins the status subscription.

Upstream: not applicable (AD5X OS specific)
